WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:06.530
The festival of dreams
to crown the strongest Pokémon Trainer...

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:10.410
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament.

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.330
The eight mighty trainers
aiming for the summit...

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.120
...have begun battling.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:20.210
At Shoot Stadium,
the site of these fateful battles,

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:26.170
Satoshi and Go met Dande’s brother, Hop,
and they ended up spectating together.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.760
The first match of the first round
was Dande VS Alan.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:35.560
Dande’s skillful battling struck down Alan,
advancing him to the semifinals.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.430
Following it is the second match...

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:43.980
...between the new Champion of Kanto and Johto, Wataru,
and the Champion of Kalos, Carne.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:50.490
Competitor Wataru and Competitor Carne
have arrived on the field.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:54.660
Which of them will end up battling
Competitor Dande in the semifinals?

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:58.750
Ms. Carne and Mr. Wataru, huh?
Which one should I cheer for?

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.120
Satoshi, you know both of them?

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.040
Yeah! One time
I even got to battle Ms. Carne.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.630
That’s incredible!

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:08.090
Even my bro
thinks highly of you...

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:11.510
You must have some knack
for getting Champions to notice you!

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.180
Wake up, meow!

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.270
More importantly, look at Carne!

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:20.480
She’s sparkling!
She’s dazzling... too dazzling!

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.270
The very image
of a star actress!

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:25.110
Humph...
A “star actress,” huh?

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.400
Well, why don’t we just see
how well she performs?

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.160
The time is come!

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.410
Trainers of Kanto!

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:37.660
Trainers of Johto!

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:40.370
Bear witness to my battle!

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:41.660
And to you, Carne!

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:46.670
As a dragon tamer, may this battle be one
my dragon brigade can be proud of!

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.880
You’ve said it well!

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.720
We are linked together by Pokémon!

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.510
And by this battle!

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:58.680
I, too, shoulder hopes and dreams...
Those of the trainers of Kalos...

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.430
...as I stand here today!

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:04.730
Mr. Wataru...
You and your Pokémon...

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:08.570
How marvelously will they shine?
I can’t wait to find out!

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.440
Then let us begin!

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.490
Sparks are flying from the get-go!

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.740
This is gonna be
a really awesome battle!

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:21.500
You may each use three Pokémon
in the first round.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.080
No limit on
switching out Pokémon.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:27.380
Whoever makes all three of their opponent’s Pokémon
unable to battle will be the winner.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:33.340
Additionally, you are allowed a single use of only one
of the following: Daimax, a Z-Move, or Mega Evolution.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:36.680
Now then, both battlers,
send your first Pokémon out onto the field!

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:38.140
Three!

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.060
Two!

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:39.850
One!

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:40.850
Go!

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:42.060
Head forth!

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:42.930
Let’s do this!

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:48.940
And the battle has begun!
Competitor Wataru chooses Kairyu!

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:52.530
His opponent, Competitor Carne,
chooses Amaruruga!

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.950
Amaruruga! Tundra Pokémon!
Rock/Ice type!

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:04.290
When gripped by rage,
it will emanate freezing air,

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.000
covering everything around it in ice!

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.000
Let the battle begin!

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.810
Let the battle begin!

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.190
Light Screen!

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:52.770
Destroyer Beam!

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:06.660
Light Screen reduced
the Destroyer Beam’s damage!

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.450
Also, firing Destroyer Beam...

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:11.670
...immobilizes the attacker
for a short while!

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:12.750
Blizzard!

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.420
It’s super effective!

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.390
Bravo.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:31.190
Good! Well done holding on!

00:05:32.270 --> 00:05:34.690
Kairyu can move again!

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:35.900
Body Press!

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:47.490
Once again, it’s super effective!

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.830
Amaruruga, stay strong!

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.130
Once more! Body Press!

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:00.510
Reflector!

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:03.090
Another defensive move!

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:08.720
Amaruruga held out
thanks to the Reflector!

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:16.560
It’s like an aurora!

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.690
Light Screen and Reflector...

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:21.360
She fortified herself
with two defense moves.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:25.870
Still, the effect of the moves
will dissipate in time.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:27.580
They’re not all-powerful.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:30.450
She must be hoping
to put pressure on Mr. Wataru, too.

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:34.460
Ms. Carne now clearly
holds the upper hand in the battle.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.630
It’s too early to call it yet.

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:39.130
Wataru won’t be fazed by this.

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:40.840
Kairyu! Twister!

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:44.680
Rock Slide!

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:49.510
Underestimate me
and you’ll be in for a shock!

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:51.890
Have a taste of my
well-trained Dragon moves!

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:05.700
Your part is over, Amaruruga!

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:13.450
Amaruruga is unable to battle!

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:19.420
Competitor Wataru takes the first win!
The terrifying power of Kairyu!

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:24.340
Placing walls before us
will only make us strike even harder!

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:28.680
Amazing!
It even endured that Rock Slide!

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:31.350
But is it going to last much longer?

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.980
Return, Amaruruga.

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:37.520
Thank you.

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:40.060
Kairyu! Return!

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:43.690
Oh! He called it back!

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:47.240
I’m counting on you,
Pumpjin!

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:54.950
Competitor Carne’s
second Pokémon is Pumpjin.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.870
And the effect of the walls is still in play!

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:02.380
Pumpjin! Pumpkin Pokémon!
Ghost/Grass type!

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:05.880
It enwraps its prey in its hairlike arms!

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.720
It sings joyfully as it observes
the suffering of its prey!

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:10.220
Pumpjin, huh?

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:12.720
Musashi caught one of those
in Kalos, meow.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.850
Pumpjin, eh...?

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:18.060
Wait...

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:23.070
Pumpjin?!
That actress lady’s got good taste!

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:26.030
You guys!
It’s a Pumpjin! A Pumpjin!

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:29.820
That’s right...

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:32.160
Come out, Gyarados!

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:37.660
Competitor Wataru’s
second Pokémon is Gyarados!

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:39.540
A red Gyarados!

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:42.590
Gyarados!
We’ll break through those walls!

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.590
Pumpjin!

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:46.380
Halloween!

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.640
What is that?!

00:08:56.640 --> 00:09:01.230
Pumpjin’s signature move.
It adds the Ghost type to its opponent!

00:09:01.230 --> 00:09:04.570
Then, if he gets hit
with a Ghost-type move...

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:05.940
It’ll be super effective!

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:08.190
Tch...
A troublesome move.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.030
Aqua Tail!

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:25.500
What power... Without the Reflector,
we might have been in trouble.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.090
The Light Screen will vanish soon.

00:09:30.050 --> 00:09:32.300
That moment will decide it!

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:34.100
Gyarados! Dragon Pulse!

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:34.930
Shadow Strike!

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:42.940
She attacks first with Shadow Strike!

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:45.400
Dealing huge damage
because of Halloween!

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.360
But!

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:57.740
The Dragon Pulse is a direct hit!

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:00.040
The Light Screen finally vanished!

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:02.500
Still standing.
In that case...

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:03.540
Ice Fang!

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:06.420
Ghost Dive!

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.590
Dragon Pulse!

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.740
Gyarados is unable to battle!

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:34.450
This time,
Competitor Carne takes the win!

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:37.370
Awesome!
They’re both awesome!

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:40.080
Incredible, Pumpjin!

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:43.290
I’m moved to tears, meow!
Even though it’s not on our side, meow!

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:46.960
That’s the first one
we’re nabbing!

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.630
Good work, Gyarados.

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:56.970
Come out, Sazandra!

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:03.980
Competitor Wataru’s
third Pokémon is Sazandra!

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:07.810
I have a strategy
for Sazandra, too.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:28.880
The second match,
Competitor Wataru VS Competitor Carne.

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:31.380
Competitor Carne uses Pumpjin.

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:33.880
Competitor Wataru uses Sazandra.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:39.220
Sazandra! Brutal Pokémon!
Evil/Dragon type!

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:40.890
It bites anything that moves!

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:45.390
There are a slew of stories about villages
that were destroyed by Sazandra!

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.190
Pumpjin...

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:47.900
Halloween!

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:56.450
I care not! Evil Pulse!

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:07.000
The Reflector’s effect has ended!

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:12.170
And because of the super effective Evil Pulse,
Pumpjin is flinching!

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:16.050
No way!
Pull it together, Pumpjin!

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:19.050
Once more! Evil Pulse!

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:28.440
Pumpjin is unable to battle!

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:33.820
We did it, Gyarados.
We owe this victory to you.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:39.660
It’s finished...

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:41.660
Hey!

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:43.700
Plug the next Pokémon!

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.910
You’re still doin’ this?

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.170
Now, Competitor Carne
is up against a wall!

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:52.420
Thank you, Pumpjin.

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:57.010
Ms. Carne’s third Pokémon
has to be...

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:00.380
It’s your time to shine...
Sirknight!

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:10.440
I knew it! Sirknight!

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:12.810
She’s finally using her ace?

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:16.190
Fairy types have an advantage over
Evil/Dragon types, after all!

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:18.440
I’ve been waiting for you,
Sirknight!

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:21.780
Let us show you
our greatest performance!

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:24.370
Sirknight! Mega Evolve!

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:58.480
All right!
It’s Mega Sirknight!

00:13:58.860 --> 00:13:59.860
Shadow Ball!

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:04.700
Tri Attack!

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.830
Offense is the greatest defense!
The first strike takes the win!

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.210
Luster Cannon!

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:19.670
Psychokinesis!

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:26.930
What?!

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:29.430
Moonforce!

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:40.360
An intense Moonforce!
Can Sazandra hold on?!

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:49.080
Sazandra is unable to battle!

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:51.620
Now Competitor Wataru
is down two as well.

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:55.960
What a back-and-forth!
The next showdown will decide the battle!

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:58.460
You fought well.

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:01.590
Leave the rest to Kairyu.

00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:02.970
Come out!

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:11.850
The final battle is
Kairyu VS Mega Sirknight!

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:15.810
Sirknight, you mustn’t let your guard down
until the very end.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:17.440
Kairyu!

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:20.360
We have not yet demonstrated
all that we can do!

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:25.360
Here goes, Kairyu!

00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:31.620
Daimax!

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:38.880
Competitor Wataru
activates Daimax!

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:48.800
Kairyu Daimaxed?!

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:51.220
It’s huge!

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:55.730
Unlike Mega Evolution,
Daimax has a time limit.

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:57.850
The whole battle
hinges on that.

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:05.740
Daimax allows Kairyu’s stamina
to go beyond its limits!

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:08.610
So you had a trick
up your sleeve...

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:12.330
But will it stand up
against my Fairy moves?

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:13.910
Moonforce!

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:18.250
Dai Ice!

00:16:32.890 --> 00:16:37.230
It held on!
It endured the Moonforce!

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:46.110
It’s hailing on the field
from the Dai Ice!

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:50.410
That’ll eat away
at their stamina bit by bit.

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:52.320
Quite the risky tactic.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:58.410
Or are you simply confident that Kairyu is
strong enough to hold on, even through hail?

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.370
Take this! Dai Attack!

00:17:05.590 --> 00:17:07.760
Shadow Ball!

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:09.760
Dai Dragoon!

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:14.300
But Dragon moves
don’t affect Fairy types!

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:16.640
No, he’s not aiming at Sirknight!

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:25.440
Incredible! The Dai Dragoon
swallowed the Shadow Ball!

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:31.740
Your plan...
I’ve figured it out.

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:39.000
Of course...
Mr. Wataru’s hanging on with his Daimax,

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.750
then he’s gonna strike
the moment it wears off!

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:47.250
Oh, and his Daimax has—

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:49.510
Destroyer Beam!

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:57.350
Checkmate!

00:17:57.350 --> 00:17:58.180
Moonforce!

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:16.450
Kairyu!

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:33.760
Kairyu is unable to battle!

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:35.890
Sirknight wins!

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:38.760
As such, the winner is
Competitor Carne!

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:44.770
Competitor Carne lands a seat
in the semifinals!

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:47.900
Thank you.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:59.370
You had me at your mercy.
Your victory was magnificent.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:04.250
I, too, greatly enjoyed
our time together.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:09.750
I look forward to seeing
how you’ll battle against Dande.

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:11.170
Indeed.

00:19:14.050 --> 00:19:17.390
A battle between Champions...
That was amazing!

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:20.350
So Mr. Dande’s facing Ms. Carne.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:23.600
Ms. Carne, and her skillful
support move combos...

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:25.520
But! Big Bro will win!

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:29.730
Ms. Carne truly is an enigma.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:32.610
Her battles change
with the Pokémon she uses.

00:19:32.610 --> 00:19:35.740
She’d call them performances
and not battles, right?

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:39.370
I can’t wait to perform
alongside her.

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:42.620
Okay!
Here’s Competitor Carne!

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:46.370
Bringing you live comments
ahead of everyone else, meow!

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:50.880
So, how are you feeling
right now, meow?

00:19:50.880 --> 00:19:53.920
Everyone in Kalos,
thank you for your support!

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:57.260
Finish the next match
with Pumpjin, ‘kay?

00:19:57.260 --> 00:19:58.510
You hear me?
With Pumpjin!

00:19:58.510 --> 00:19:59.970
With <i>Pumpjin!</i>

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:04.140
Mr. Wataru!

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:06.810
Hey, Satoshi.

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:09.480
My battles end here.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:11.360
Hang in there.

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:15.240
Satoshi.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:17.150
Iris!

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:18.530
You’re finally up!

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:24.580
Right now, I’m just so nervous...
And I’m so fired up...

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:26.960
...and I just wanna get out there
and let loose!

00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:30.460
You’re up against Ms. Shirona.
Go at her with everything you’ve got!

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:34.050
Yeah! I’m gonna win a match
before you, Satoshi!

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:35.590
Ooh, now you’ve said it!

00:20:35.590 --> 00:20:36.720
Okay, I’ll be back soon!

00:20:36.720 --> 00:20:39.090
Pikachu, you cheer for me, too!

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:46.600
The third match of the first round.

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:50.350
The Champion of Sinnoh,
Competitor Shirona, is on the field.

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:55.360
Her opponent is the Champion of Isshu,
Competitor Iris.

00:20:55.360 --> 00:21:01.280
This is a clash between the dignified
queen of Sinnoh and a young Champion.

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:06.790
This battle is a 3v3! Both battlers,
send your first Pokémon out onto the field!

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:07.750
Three!

00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:08.620
Two!

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:09.580
One!

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:10.620
Go!

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:13.210
Come out, Doryuzu!

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:16.460
Emerge from the waves, Toritodon!

00:21:22.470 --> 00:21:24.430
Ms. Shirona’s using Toritodon?

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:26.430
And the other Pokémon is...

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:27.970
It’s Doryuzu!

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:39.320
The Masters Tournament...
